#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/az.rc -- Azerbaijani (Latin script, Azerbaijan), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "az"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. Left to right, Latin script with the letters ə ğ ı İ ö ü ç ş:
// the dotted and the dotless i are different letters, in capitals too (İ / I). Quotes are the
// guillemets «», as in the Russian text; the polite "siz" form addresses the reader (a Turkic
// language has no grammatical gender, so the voice of the author and of the reader need none).
// No suffix is put on a substitution ({0}, {1}): the vowel harmony of a variable cannot be known.
// The key names stay in Latin letters, as the hotkey field prints them (RULES 4).
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Azerbaijani (Latin) — `[general] language = "az"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
